mode: "100644"
text: "# The Daily & Weekly Routine\n\nThe actual cadence. Engagement is the highest-return activity in social (replying lifts engagement on\nevery platform), but only if it's a **habit, not a heroic burst.** This is the operating system that\nturns the craft (`reply-and-comment-writer`) into a repeatable routine.\n\n> Re-verify timing specifics quarterly; the structure (windows + golden hour, batched not all-day) is\n> durable.\n\n## The principle: windows, not all-day\n\nDon't graze notifications all day — it wrecks focus and burns you out. **Batch engagement into a few\ndedicated windows.** A common, sustainable shape:\n\n- **~20 minutes in the morning** and **~20 minutes in the afternoon** (adjust to your capacity).\n- Plus a **golden-hour pass** right after each post publishes.\n\n## The golden hour (non-negotiable)\n\nThe **first ~15–20 minutes** after a post goes live is the highest-leverage engagement window — early\nreplies build the comment thread and signal the algorithm, lifting reach. **Post when you can be\npresent**, and spend that window replying to early comments. (This is why you schedule posts for times\nyou can show up — see `the-scheduling-engagement-flywheel.md`.)\n\n## Order of operations (each window)\n\nSpend the time in priority order (full triage in `triage-priorities-and-goals.md`):\n\n1. **Reply to comments** on your recent/fresh posts (golden hour first).\n2. **Respond to DMs** — where relationships and conversions happen.\n3. **Handle anything negative/urgent** quickly.\n4. **Proactive commenting** — add value on 3–5 posts from **ICP, peers, and niche leaders** (borrows\n   their audience; strategic commenting in `reply-and-comment-writer`).\n\nThe agent **drafts** these (in brand voice, via `reply-and-comment-writer`); the **human reviews and\nposts** them in-app.\n\n## A worked daily template (solo brand, ~40 min/day)\n\n- **Morning (20 min):** reply to overnight comments (5) → reply to DMs (3) → 3 proactive comments on\n  ICP/leader posts.\n- **At publish time (golden hour, ~15 min):** reply to every early comment on the new post; ask a\n  question back to keep threads alive.\n- **Afternoon (20 min):** clear new comments/DMs → 2–3 more proactive comments → note any recurring\n  question to turn into content.\n\nScale up/down by capacity (see below).\n\n## Weekly rhythm\n\n- **Once a week (~30 min):** find 10–15 accounts/threads worth engaging (ICP, peers, leaders) for the\n  week; note recurring questions to convert into posts (→ `caption-writer`); skim what landed\n  (natively — no WoopSocial analytics) and do more of it.\n- **Protect the boundaries** (`sustainability-and-boundaries.md`).\n\n## Scale the routine to reality\n\n- **Time:** an hour a day is a healthy ceiling for most solo brands; 40 min works; even 2×10 min beats\n  sporadic bursts. **Consistency > intensity.**\n- **Platforms:** more platforms = more time. **Concentrate where your audience actually is** rather than\n  spreading thin across every platform you publish to.\n- **Capacity:** when busy, shrink the windows but **keep the golden hour** — it's the highest return.\n"
